-# Under the title of a contest-scoped report: what the contest fixes (its
-# problems, its students, its window) and the way back to the filter cards.
-# Also the notice when ?contest= named a contest the viewer cannot manage:
-# the id is ignored and the filter cards stay in force. Local: path (this
-# report's page path, for the clear link).
- if @report_contest
  - c = @report_contest
  - stop_format = c.stop.to_date == c.start.to_date ? '%H:%M' : '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M'
  .card.shadow-sm.mb-3#report-contest-scope
    .card-body.py-2.d-flex.align-items-center.flex-wrap.gap-2
      %span.mi.text-primary emoji_events
      .flex-grow-1
        %span.fw-bold.font-monospace= c.name
        = "— #{pluralize(c.problems.count, 'problem')} · #{pluralize(c.students.count, 'student')} · #{c.start.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')}–#{c.stop.strftime(stop_format)}"
        - if c.per_user_windows?
          plus each student's own start offset and extra time
      = link_to path, class: 'btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary d-inline-flex align-items-center gap-1' do
        %span.mi.md-18 close
        Clear contest
- elsif @report_contest_ignored
  .alert.alert-warning.border-0.shadow-sm.mb-3.d-flex.align-items-start.gap-2{role: 'alert'}
    %span.mi.text-warning warning
    .small
      Contest ##{@report_contest_ignored} is not one you can manage, so it was ignored — the filters below are in force.
